	About the XHack game
	--------------------

        XHack  is a  Dungeons and Dragons  like game, where you   (the
        adventurer) descend  into the depths of the dungeon  in search
        of the Shattered Statue.  On the way  you will find useful (or
        useless)  items   (quite possibly with magic properties),  and
        assorted monsters. You attack a monster by trying to move into
        the space a monster is in (but often it is much wiser to leave
        it alone).

                XHack was created in C++ language using the X11 window
        system as a graphics interface. XHack has three major parts:
          	(1) XHack Server 
          	(2) XHack Client
          	(3) XHack Communication Protocol.

                XHack is inspired by Hack,  NetHack,  Rouge and  Moria
        games with two major changes: First, the game is designed with
        a graphical interface that replaces the text orientation of
        the above mentioned games, and Second,  the XHack  is designed
        to be a multi-user game where several players can  interact in
        a single game.

                To play the XHack,  a client  (player)  should execute
        the client program on his host with a parameter that tells the
        client program  where to  connect to  (the server's host)  and
        while the server is running.  The  client p rogram requires an
        X11 work station display.
                To run the server on any host, just execute the server
        program  (called 'server')  from  its proper  directory.   The
        server runs until it is killed or ordered to exit from a "god"
        client (a client who have the "god"'s password)
                All connection between the server and the clients is
        done via the internet.

